{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/903708-saving-the-unicorn-thread-from-the-fenrir","id":903708,"title":"Saving the Unicorn Thread from the Fenrir","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-30T12:19:39-07:00","id":903708,"title":"Saving the Unicorn Thread from the Fenrir","content":"I wanted to comment on the Fenrir debate that is currently invading the heretical thoughts on Unicorn thread.<br /> <br /> There is an debate on the races and ethnic make up of the Fenrir right now in that thread where people were debating how many PoC would be in the tribe due to its origins in N. Europe. One thing I did want to point out is remember that the Norse were famous for travel historically and look at how far they did range.<br /> In cannon there is the Ymir's Sweat Lodge, which are Fenrir of Native American descent. Basically the Get came to North America and many of them stayed. In the 1st ed book they were looked down on as &quot;impure&quot; but revised took a spin on them I ran with in one of my games. In revised they are a welcome addition to the tribe and the Fenrir like to insinuate that the people the Fenrir bred with were not kin to the Wendigo (too weak according to them) but instead the proud Croatan, and that its this camp that is the legacy of that tribe and their great sacrifice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 05-30-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T12:54:18-07:00","id":903722,"title":"","content":"It is stated in W20 that they &quot;(...) do not commonly make themselves (or their lineage) known, as both the Fenrir and Wendigo have been known to look unkindly upon those who come from \u201csullied\u201d breeding.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, even if you run them as welcome, i always liked their concept, how often did you use them and how where the plot lines with them involved?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:04:43-07:00","id":903727,"title":"","content":"Well to see they went back to 1st ed on that group is a huge disappointment in my opinion. I considered their acceptance to be one of the big signs of washing away the 1st ed nazi stuff that I was not particularly fond of either. I try not to over use them, because I don't wan them to seem like half of the tribe, but I tend to have them pop up from time to time. I like using them to highlight the complexities of both Fenrir culture, but also I had some players with relatively skewed views of Native people. The npc I used the most often saw himself as Fenrir first, and that he just happened to come from a different human background than many of his tribe mates. A lot of his plot were more to help point out the difference between what your human culture is, and what your tribe is. To remind people that the Fenrir are not Vikings, merely a separate culture that was highly involved with them, but was not bound by them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:16:39-07:00","id":903734,"title":"","content":"They surely kicked major ass as well, because else they sound a bit rainbowfamilyesque while still being bland. Personally i loved the idea of a political intrigue and the lineage of the werwolf being a secret that some idiot PC would try to use against him/her. Endless possibilities could arise from it, from the NPC going ham on the PC, to self proclaim it in pride and challenges as well as pure hate and the gaining of an enemy flaw...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T13:43:03-07:00","id":903756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/903708-saving-the-unicorn-thread-from-the-fenrir?p=903734#post903734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They surely kicked major ass as well, because else they sound a bit rainbowfamilyesque while still being bland. Personally i loved the idea of a political intrigue and the lineage of the werwolf being a secret that some idiot PC would try to use against him/her. Endless possibilities could arise from it, from the NPC going ham on the PC, to self proclaim it in pride and challenges as well as pure hate and the gaining of an enemy flaw...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'm understanding what you mean...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T14:08:44-07:00","id":903771,"title":"","content":"Well i hope that the NPC had another task in your story and not only to educate the players. What where his goals, what is his character? Was a wild and savage or was he sneaky and strong or was he intelligent and what ever? What was his role in to the pack or the story. Did the players like him, maybe somebody challenged him? <br /> <br /> Stuff like that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T14:42:16-07:00","id":903784,"title":"","content":"His pack was called &quot;the Vanguard&quot; and were the caern's first response team. He liked the idea of being the first in, and being the one the Sept relied on if it seemed like a mission that could go array. He saw having minimal information before hand as a testament to his true potential. He took an interest in the pack because he saw them as too hesitant to engage in combat (they were huge on planning, and information gathering, at times I felt a little toooo much). Most of the players liked him with the exception of the Fenrir raggy in the group (he respected her the least because he saw her as too combat avoidant and expected more of her.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how secret lineages in this case could work too well (which is why i'm not big on the idea of them being all &quot;hush hush&quot; in W20) since there's no reason that their human heritage wouldn't be quite visible (we are talking about the possibility of no caucasian blood for several generations), and I'd see not relating their tribal affiliation as probably a big social no no in Garou culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 05-31-2016, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T14:54:18-07:00","id":903789,"title":"","content":"While I understand the need to show immediate disdain for anything flavored nazi, the swords of Heimdall DO have a purpose in the game. Each tribe has that one camp that's fallen to one extreme. The glass walkers have their techno dogs, the swords work much the same way. It's a sign of what can happen and should be an example of what not to do. I'd advocate utilizing them as a new brand of fallen garou, their own tribe as in the apocalypse book. <br /> <br /> One can find use in anything, but I find the blind disdain a bit disturbing, as it seems like instead of actually forming ideas people are foaming at the muzzle and moving lock step with the social agenda. In short, y'all are thinking too much. <br /> <br /> And Celt I agree with ya, I love the individual mix breed tribes! I love originality and off shoots, and apocalypse's tribal set up allows for that if you're ambitious enough. Forsaken does too, but not to the same extent, being based on religious ideology and not genetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:07:45-07:00","id":903796,"title":"","content":"For me I was more stating that the idea that the Fenrir would have interbred with the peoples where they traveled to makes too much sense. Its not a matter of being &quot;diverse for diversities sake&quot; or &quot;PC&quot; so much as following logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:18:05-07:00","id":903799,"title":"","content":"Oh well yeah. But at some point they'd stop genetically being fenrir. I would think the ymirs sweat group would look totally native with fairer skin. Using the Rus as an example, when they traveled to Russia and formed the country they interbred with the local Slavs and essentially became Slavic within what... 150 years? Same deal with the Normans, although one Germanic group is arguably the same when compared to the folks of the Croatan or wendigo. <br /> <br /> Which brings up the main point, there could be a variety of diverse skin tones in the fenrir based on linneage to fenris, however I might argue there would be a stigma among homid garou. Lupus wouldn't give two shits. <br /> <br /> We're assuming genetics is a reason for joining as well, when one should be able to prove to a totem they're worth while, and id imagine most fenrir to be accepting of anyone who made it past the trials in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:33:32-07:00","id":903807,"title":"","content":"I don't see it as &quot;at some point they'd cease to be Fenrir&quot; if they were carrying with them the central cultural themes of that tribe. Tribes don't have to be genetic at all (CoG, Black Fury, Glass Walkers, ect.) so I don't see why the Ymir's sweat would need to be &quot;lighter skinned&quot;. Think about how far back Viking colonization of North America was. I think that would vary based on the individual characters made and their back stories (1 could be mostly caucasian in ancestry and look it while another realistically might not have any blood since the Nordic colonization that founded the bloodline).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":".  I couldn't spell to save my life for some reason 05-31-2016, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:40:13-07:00","id":903810,"title":"","content":"We're saying the same thing but splitting hairs on dialogue here. When I say fenrir I'm thinking physical not spirtual. Like they wouldn't have the physical Nordic blood (at least for appearances) but they'd still have fenrir customs. <br /> <br /> Is there a book on them and what aspects of what cultures they adapt? Or is that largely up to us?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:48:24-07:00","id":903813,"title":"","content":"They get a little blurb like they are a camp in each tribe book. I was amused with Revised making a comment that the Croatan's blood lives on the Fenrir because I also like the idea of the conflict over who is closer to Middle Brother. Imagine the Wendigo hearing that claim (Ok Crytash I now see your point, and yes that has come up in game too....the NPC did love making those claims around the Wendigo).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:52:35-07:00","id":903817,"title":"","content":"What I wouldn't mind seeing in a 4th edition, assuming it's after the apocalypse like vampire, would be a blending of tribes. Cultural diffusion. So ymirs sweat would wind up being a tribe where fenrir and wendigo might dissapear. Course that wouldn't go over so well with some but hey, who knows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T15:54:20-07:00","id":903818,"title":"","content":"Could be interesting in a more integrated world....though I almost feel it should be more Fianna/Fenrir lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T17:12:23-07:00","id":903859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/903708-saving-the-unicorn-thread-from-the-fenrir?p=903810#post903810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're saying the same thing but splitting hairs on dialogue here. When I say fenrir I'm thinking physical not spirtual. Like they wouldn't have the physical Nordic blood (at least for appearances) but they'd still have fenrir customs.<br /> <br /> Is there a book on them and what aspects of what cultures they adapt? Or is that largely up to us?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like a Pure Breed argument, but that Trait has nothing to do with human appearance anymore, only wolf appearance, and as long as they're Garou of a given tribe sticking together, Pure Breed will rise. If you keep getting accepted by the totem and have a lot of Kin among people that weren't formerly associated with the Fenrir, you remain the great grey wolves of the north.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:01:30-07:00","id":904122,"title":"","content":"Personally, the issue with Fenrir is complex. Being from Finland, and being pretty ware of the political and cultural contexts of Scandinavia(+Finland) also affects my view of the tribe.<br /> <br /> Here's how I see it, the Sons of Heimindal make sense within the context the camp arose. It brought fort elements of desperation of youth and the ideas of the pre-WW2 Germany. These elements are still present in the world, of course. But the camp itself should be very VERY much a secret now, if it still exists.<br /> <br /> However, it was the more broader view of all Fenrir being racist and racial purists, that really is the issue most of us here have. First of all, I understand that when WtA first came out, the setting wasn't as refined nor the world like it is today. Each tribe was a broad stereotype, fenrir being the tough nordic warriors who were germany-based and racist. Given the other content oWoD had at the time, it was hardly the worst thing running around the setting. However, it was based on a stereotype that was more American than European.<br /> <br /> Also, 'looking fenrir' doesn't really work. While there are blond haired blue eyed people here, there are as many darker haired and green or hazel eyed people as well. Nevermind the sami up very north. And the wolves? Most have ticked and reddish coat, rather than a pale gray one. And this has been the case for centuries. Also, those that -do- have the right looks look more like this: <a href=\"http://img.yle.fi/radio/yleradio1/ohjelmat/lukupiiri/article8369661.ece/ALTERNATES/w960/seitseman-veljesta-YleAntero-Tenhunen-1443771861-9149.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://img.yle.fi/radio/yleradio1/oh...71861-9149.jpg</a><br /> <br /> Than the typical viking view. At least here in insular Finland. For Norway, Sweden, Denmark and Iceland, their people sailed a lot and so had a much more diverse genepool.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:32:44-07:00","id":904652,"title":"","content":"There's more to appearance differentiation between the peoples then just hair color and eye color. A native individual from the time of norse (very brief) colonization would look physically different from the Norse beyond simply hair and eyes. At any rate, thinking about these individual groups makes me think instead of camps they should develop into micro tribes. Isn't that how the singing dogs work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:37:19-07:00","id":904655,"title":"","content":"I'd support them...get Turtle to return...similar to how Lion stuck it out with Gryphon.....SO any ideas on how a Fenrir could wake Turtle up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:55:24-07:00","id":904664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/903708-saving-the-unicorn-thread-from-the-fenrir?p=904655#post904655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd support them...get Turtle to return...similar to how Lion stuck it out with Gryphon.....SO any ideas on how a Fenrir could wake Turtle up?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, bring back the Croatan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T20:38:47-07:00","id":904686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</stron